*                                                                          *
*   Author(s)     : Louis T Steinhil                                       *
*   Created Date  : 2025-07-16                                             *
*   Last Modified : 2026-07-24                                             *
*                                                                          *
*   Description   : Routes the Banquet 0x0BDD item-color list into a       *
*                   bounded EXE-resident table. New ICL2 trailers color    *
*                   producer surfaces by ItemId first; legacy ItemName     *
*                   records remain for old clients and final text-only     *
*                   surfaces. This patch's rendering contract is           *
*                   non-negotiable: grade mode                           *
*                   conditionally coalesces the native post-grade         *
*                   endpoint so one complete decorated UTF-16 title is    *
*                   drawn and the grade color always wins over the item   *
*                   database. Inventory matching accepts only anchored    *
*                   space-quantity, slotless-colon, and slotted-colon     *
*                   forms. Matched shadows and grade quantity tails are   *
*                   omitted; no draw state crosses TextOutW calls.        *
*                   Runtime labels follow stock [D]/[C]/[B]/[A] or the    *
*                   active custom map. Emoji and EXTN text remain         *
*                   explicitly excluded.                                 *
*                   Targets: 2025-07-16 and 2026-02-19 Ragexe.            *
*                                                                          *
\**************************************************************************/

